   "line": 7,
   "text": "Closer poles make the notch narrower. The bandwidth is the width of the notch, in hertz, between the two tones on either side that it passes at seventy-one percent. Radius point nine gives two hundred sixty-six hertz. Point nine eight gives fifty-one. Bandwidth times decay time, in seconds, stays near one point four six.",
